  "finding": "MarketDataLoaderBase._normalize casts volume to int64. Symbols whose stored volume is fractional lose the fraction on every bar, and a bar under 1.0 unit with real trades becomes volume 0. Symbols already stored as int64 are unaffected, so the defect is invisible on exactly the symbols one would test first.",
  "lab_consequence": "reading the parquet directly preserves the stored resolution; panel.normalize_numeric_dtypes coerces to float64 on read so a feature's dtype never depends on which month it came from",
